    <h2>How Reem works</h2>
    <p class="intro-wide">Most of what brings people here was learned somewhere, and learned for
    a reason. All three methods start from that, and none of them asks you to push through.</p>
    {#- Only the three-word heading was clickable on a card whose whole body
        is about that method. The card is the link now. -#}
    <div class="pathways">
      <a href="/approach/narm/">
        <h3>NARM</h3>
        <p>An invitation to get curious about a pattern rather than to fight it. Where did I
        learn this? What was it doing for me then? And if I am present enough to notice it
        happening, what choice do I actually have? The answers tend to arrive through the felt
        sense rather than through analysis, which is why the work is slower than advice and why
        it holds.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/ifs-informed-emdr/">
        <h3>IFS-informed EMDR</h3>
        <p>The protective parts of you are consulted before anything is processed, and most of
        the emphasis sits in the preparation, where that agreement gets built. It is weighted
        toward stabilization rather than excavation, which is what acute stress, ongoing stress,
        overwhelm and loss actually need.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/somatic-experiencing/">
        <h3>Somatic Experiencing</h3>
        <p>Shock trauma met a little at a time, slow and gentle, building your window of
        tolerance rather than testing it. A nervous system learns resilience at the pace it can
        hold, and not faster.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/therapy/walk-and-talk/">
        <h3>Outdoors, when it helps</h3>
        <p>Reem teaches effortless self-care through walk and mindful therapy, outdoors, which
        for some people is the difference between talking about something and being able to stay
        with it.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="intro-wide">For therapists: she has supervised
    <a href="/for-therapists/lpc-supervision/">LPC Associates</a> since {{ site.supervisorSince }},
    online anywhere in Texas, and runs
    <a href="/for-therapists/retreats-training/">mindful trail retreats</a> for interns,
    associates and therapists, where the subject is being present and what gets in the way of
    it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

